#!/bin/sh
# Release environment (DOS-M09-007 FR-17).
#
# `mix release` defaults RELEASE_DISTRIBUTION to "sname", which starts epmd and
# brings up a distributed Erlang node with the cookie baked into the image at
# releases/COOKIE. Nothing in this application asks for that: DNSCluster is
# started with `:ignore` because DNS_CLUSTER_QUERY is unset, PubSub is local,
# and no code calls Node or :rpc. It was on purely because it is the default.
#
# Distribution is the remote-inspection surface FR-17 requires disabled. It was
# never reachable from the internet — Fly publishes only the ports in
# [http_service], so epmd and the distribution port were confined to the
# organisation's private network — but "not currently reachable" is a property
# of the network, not of the application, and it is the kind of thing that
# changes without anyone revisiting this.
#
# Turning it off also removes the release cookie's reason to exist, and with it
# the question of whether a cookie baked into a published image is a secret.
#
# The cost: `flyctl ssh console` can no longer attach a remote shell to the
# running node. `bin/digital_oil_sticker rpc` still works, because it runs in
# the container rather than over distribution. That is the right trade for an
# app whose operator rule (FR-18) is that console access is for diagnosing the
# application, never for inspecting a live session.
export RELEASE_DISTRIBUTION=none
